note seed/node/tests/nodedrv.om: helpers for the Omega Node acceptance drivers (view-prep.om,
note view-accept.om): the DRA-291 fixture (prep: what view-prep.py did), node and fake-serve
note processes, omnode-op calls and their JSON answers, output lines, the journal and the
note listening check. Composition: om2, seed/json/json.om, seed/node/tests/drv.om, this unit, the
note driver's main unit. Names: nd_* functions, nd* globals and texts.
note The context buffer cx (65536 bytes) holds path slots, slot i at i*4096 with its length in
note ndl[i]: [0] BUILD, [1] OMC, [2] ROUND40, [3] OUTDIR, [4] BASE (the scenario directory), [5]
note scratch path, [6] the node command "PROGRAM [MODE...]" (nd_set; nd_node), [7] the op capture
note file. Bytes 32768..65535 hold the prepared objectives, one newline-terminated line each:
note ndl[8] their byte count, ndl[9] their number. Limits: 6 argument slots per function (an
note unsized view/edit costs 2, a sized one 1), so js is passed as jsmaxn-sized where needed.

global ndl ulong 16
note ndpid, ndpst: tracked child processes (at most 16, ndpn[0] of them): the pid, and its status
note (-1 while it runs; dv_wstat code once reaped, so a finished process keeps its status).
global ndpid long 16
global ndpst long 16
global ndpn ulong 2
note ndr: the last op call: [0] its exit status (-110 at the 30 s deadline, other negative values:
note spawn errors), [1] 1 when its stdout parsed as JSON onto the caller's js and tp (root token 0).
global ndr long 4
note ndoa, ndon[0]: the op numbers after the port and word (nd_args, nd_argx): ndon[0] of ndoa.
global ndoa long 16
global ndon ulong 2
note ndbad[0]: set to 1 when an accessor meets a missing or mistyped value; callers clear it.
global ndbad ulong 1
note ndport: [0] the last fake-serve port, [1] the last node's view port, [2] 1 when that node's
note view came up (its CWV line seen while it still ran).
global ndport long 4
note ndob: the prepared objectives' original values, four each: kind code (1 add, 2 mul, 3 loop,
note 0 other), k, n, a. ndrun: their run tokens in the fixture (at most 128), ndrn[0] the count.
global ndob long 512
global ndrun ulong 128
global ndrn ulong 1
note ndw: the buffered writer: [0] bytes buffered, [1] descriptor + 1 (0 none), [2] counting mode
note (1: nd_wb counts into [3] and writes nothing), [3] the count. ndwe[0]: the first write error.
global ndw ulong 4
global ndwe long 1
note ndlc[0]: listening entries counted by nd_lsnf.
global ndlc ulong 1
note ndev, ndevn[0]: a list of up to 4096 events of four numbers each (the full scenario's own
note job events, or any caller's list).
global ndev long 16384
global ndevn ulong 1

text ndsel "final-selected.json"
text ndkjob "job"
text ndkpath "path"
text ndkflt "fault"
text ndkkind "kind"
text ndkstyl "style"
text ndkk "k"
text ndkn "n"
text ndka "a"
text ndkbrok "broken"
text ndkturn "turns"
text ndkraw "raw"
text ndkstat "state"
text ndkprom "prompt"
text ndkpass "pass"
text ndmiss "missing"
text ndadd "add"
text ndmul "mul"
text ndloop "loop"
text ndroot "root"
text ndrjobs "root/jobs"
text ndrsl "/root/"
text ndwork "work"
text ndjour "journal"
text ndjfile "journal/journal"
text ndobjs "objs.txt"
text ndexp "expect.json"
text ndmap "map"
text ndflog "fake.log"
text ndfake "fake-serve"
text ndinfer "infer"
text ndtool "tool"
text ndop "op"
text ndopout ".op.out"
text ndportw "PORT"
text ndcwv "CWV "
text ndview "view"
text ndcmd "cmd"
text ndwx "x"
text ndout ".out"
text nderr ".err"
text ndnone "None"
text ndtcp "/proc/net/tcp"
text ndtcp6 "/proc/net/tcp6"
note Keys and values of omnode-op answers (seed/node/view.om).
text ndklay "layout"
text ndkinc "incarnation"
text ndkver "version"
text ndksnce "since"
